CommE5070 HW1 — Singer Classification — inference instructions
================================================================

Setup
-----
    pip install -r requirements.txt

(torch>=2.6 is required — some pretrained checkpoints used by two of the
models fail to load under HF's safetensors-only `torch.load` policy on
older torch.)

Data
----
Point everything at your local copy of the artist20 dataset (same layout as
provided: `train.json`, `val.json`, `train_val/<artist>/<album>/*.mp3`,
`test/*.mp3`). Build the manifest once:

    python -m src.data.prepare_index --data_root /path/to/artist20 --out_dir data/index

Running inference (the graded submission)
-------------------------------------------
Per the TA's clarification on NTU Cool (see `TA_discussion.md` #4 — Task 2
requires training your own encoder *and* classifier from scratch; a
pretrained encoder, frozen or fine-tuned, is only valid as a baseline
comparison, not the graded submission), the graded Task-2 submission is a
**weighted-average ensemble of 5 from-scratch models**: `sota_crnn`×2 +
`sota_crnn_wide`×1 + `short_chunk_cnn`×1 + `sota_crnn_norm`×1 (weights
grid-searched on val, see `results/ensemble2/ensemble_result.json`). Val:
**85.3% top1 / 90.5% top3**, the best result among from-scratch-eligible
options in this project (individually, the strongest single model is
`sota_crnn_wide` at 80.5%/92.2% — a capacity-scaled variant of `sota_crnn`).
Reproduce the submitted `R13921031.json`:

    python -m src.ensemble --data_index_dir data/index \
        --models confound_crnn:results/confound_crnn/best.pt \
                 crnn_zain:results/crnn_zain/best.pt \
                 sota_crnn:results/sota_crnn/best.pt \
                 sota_crnn_wide:results/sota_crnn_wide/best.pt \
                 short_chunk_cnn:results/short_chunk_cnn/best.pt \
                 se_resnet:results/se_resnet/best.pt \
                 fgnl:results/fgnl/best.pt \
                 sample_cnn:results/sample_cnn/best.pt \
                 sota_crnn_norm:results/sota_crnn_norm/best.pt \
        --out_dir results/ensemble2 --max_weight 2 \
        --test_out_path R13921031.json

(`--models` includes 4 more candidates the grid search is free to weight to
0 — it found the 5-model combination above on its own.) No pretrained
weights are downloaded for any component — every parameter in every model
was trained on Artist20's train split. Output is
`{"001": [top1, top2, top3], ...}` for all 233 test tracks, top-3 in
descending confidence order, matching the assignment's schema.

For a single-model (simpler, no ensemble) reproduction, use `sota_crnn_wide`
alone the same way as any other model below.

Other from-scratch models (`sota_crnn`, `sota_crnn_wide`, `confound_crnn`,
`crnn_zain`, `fgnl`, `short_chunk_cnn`, `sample_cnn`, `se_resnet`,
`sota_crnn_norm`/`_attn`/`_narrow`/`_dropblock`/`_supcon`/`_swa`/
`_ssl_finetune`, `confound_crnn_vocals`/`_remix` — ablations) can be run the
same way by swapping `--model`/`--checkpoint`; see `MATERIALS.md` for the
full results table and ablation-by-ablation writeup (12 variants of the
winning architecture — capacity, pooling, normalization, optimizer,
regularization, and SSL-pretraining ablations, each measured not assumed).

**Baselines using pretrained encoders** (`ssl_frontend` = frozen MERT + a
trained head, `speaker_frontend` = frozen ECAPA-TDNN speaker embedding + a
trained head) are included for comparison only, per the assignment doc's own
"Baseline 1 (optional)" framing and the TA's clarification above — not the
graded submission, even though `speaker_frontend` scores far higher (95.2%
top1) than any from-scratch model. Runnable the same way (`--model
speaker_frontend --checkpoint results/speaker_frontend/best.pt`); see
`MATERIALS.md` for the full comparison and the deep-dive on why the gap is so
large.

See `README.md` for the full command list (training, evaluation, t-SNE,
mel-spectrogram demo) and `MATERIALS.md` for every model's measured results.

Task 1 (traditional ML)
------------------------
    python -m src.classical_ml --data_index_dir data/index --out_dir results/task1

Fits kNN/SVM(RBF)/RandomForest on hand-crafted features and reports
confusion matrix + top1/top3 on the val set (no test-set submission for
this task, per the assignment's Task 1 spec).

Notes for reproduction
-----------------------
- `ssl_frontend` and `speaker_frontend` need `torch>=2.6` specifically
  (see above); the from-scratch CRNN family (`confound_crnn`, `crnn_zain`,
  `sota_crnn`, `fgnl`) has no such constraint.
- All models chunk audio into 5s windows and predict per-track by averaging
  chunk-level softmax probabilities — see `src/data/dataset.py` and
  `src/evaluate.py`.
- Full experiment log, decisions, and citations: `EXPERIMENT_LOG.md` and
  `MATERIALS.md`.
